---
import Service from '../layouts/Service.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'What railing styles do you install?', a: 'Our go-to is Fortress FE26 aluminum in Black Sand. We also install frameless glass, cable, horizontal rod, Wild Hog mesh, privacy, composite and vinyl railing. Each has a different look, price and level of view-through.' },
  { q: 'How tall does a deck railing need to be?', a: 'Residential code generally requires guards at least 36 inches tall on decks more than 30 inches above grade, with openings smaller than 4 inches. We build to your city’s code.' },
  { q: 'Can you replace just my railing?', a: 'Yes. Railing replacement is a quick way to modernize an older deck, as long as the posts and framing are sound.' },
];
---
<Service
  slug="porches-railings"
  name="Porches & Railings"
  title="Front Porch & Deck Railing Installation in Utah County | TC Decks"
  description="Front porches, stairs and deck railing in Saratoga Springs and Utah County. Fortress aluminum, glass, cable and privacy railing. Free estimate."
  h1="Front porches and deck railings"
  lead="A new front porch adds curb appeal and a place to sit, and the right railing can change the whole look of a deck. We build both."
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <h2>Front porches</h2>
  <p>We build and extend front porches with composite decking, wide stairs and railing that match your home. Expanding a narrow builder porch is one of the most noticeable upgrades you can make to the front of a house.</p>
  <Photo src="/images/ideas/front-porch-white-railing" alt="Front porch with white railing and gray composite steps" />

  <h2>Railing options</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Style</th><th>Look</th><th>Good for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Fortress FE26 aluminum (our go-to)</td><td>Slim, modern, Black Sand finish</td><td>Durability, clean lines</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Frameless glass</td><td>Completely open</td><td>Unblocked views</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cable</td><td>Nearly invisible</td><td>Mountain and lake views</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Composite</td><td>Matches composite decking</td><td>A coordinated look</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vinyl</td><td>Classic white</td><td>Traditional homes, budget</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Stairs</h2>
  <p>Wide landings, picture-framed treads and stair lighting make stairs safer and better looking. We build stairs to code with proper rise, run and graspable handrails.</p>
  <p>See photos of every railing style in our <a href="/design-ideas/railings">railing ideas</a>.</p>
</Service>
